shower.<br> -I get dressed.<br> -I eat breakfast.<br> -I go to work.<br>  <br><span class=\"strong\">Note: </span>When talking about daily routines you use the <u>Simple Present tense.</u> <br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "John doesn't wake up at 5:30 a.m."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The driver drops off his kids at school."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't work on a cruise ship."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "all sorts of"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "all kinds of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I get to meet all sorts of people."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "glamorous"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "beautiful; lovely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your job sounds glamorous."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "roughly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "about; approximately"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I work roughly 9 hours a day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to drop off"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take someone to a place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I drop off my kids at school."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get a chance "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have an opportunity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I get a chance to meet many people."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le15